# Gemfile.lock is intentionally tracked here: the GitHub Pages build runs
# `bundler-cache`, so committing the lock keeps CI resolving exactly the gem
# versions the site was verified with (and stops the file showing up as an
# "untracked but present on the remote" oddity).
